    "v2_accordion_QgWf3B": {
      "type": "v2_accordion",
      "blocks": {
        "accordion_row_NTEyk8": {
          "type": "accordion_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What qualifications do I need to become a Personal Trainer in the UK?",
            "row_content": "<p>To work legally and professionally as a Personal Trainer in the UK, you need a Level 3 Diploma in Personal Training (or equivalent) that is Ofqual-regulated and endorsed by CIMSPA (Chartered Institute for the Management of Sport and Physical Activity), the leading professional body for the sector. Many providers (including StudyActive) bundle this with a Level 2 Certificate in Gym Instructing as a combined course, since Level 2 is the prerequisite for Level 3.<br/><br/>•\tNo prior degree or formal academic qualifications are required — just a passion for fitness and basic English/maths literacy.<br/>•\tCIMSPA endorsement ensures your qualification meets professional standards, making you eligible for gym employment, freelance work, and insurance.<br/>•\tOptional but highly recommended: Join CIMSPA as a member for CPD points, professional recognition, and networking (not mandatory for basic PT work).<br/><br/>Our Study Active Personal Trainer course meets these exact standards and prepares you fully for the industry.<br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_row_w94eBY": {
          "type": "accordion_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do I need prior experience or a Level 2 qualification before starting a Personal Trainer course?",
            "row_content": "<p>No prior fitness experience is required to enrol - many successful PTs start from scratch. However, most Level 3 courses (including ours) require or include a Level 2 Gym Instructing qualification as a foundation.</p><p><br/>If you're completely new, opt for a combined Level 2 + Level 3 package (like Study Active offers). This covers gym floor basics before advancing to client programming, assessments, and business skills. You can complete everything in one streamlined programme.<br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_row_gjjh3n": {
          "type": "accordion_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How long does it take to qualify as a Personal Trainer?",
            "row_content": "<p>Timelines vary by study mode and your availability:</p><p><br/>•\tFull-time/intensive: 4–12 weeks (classroom or accelerated online).<br/>•\tPart-time/flexible (most popular): 3–6 months (ideal for working adults).<br/>•\tSelf-paced online with practical workshops: Up to 9–12 months.</p><p><br/>Study Active's blended course typically takes 3–6 months, with lifetime resource access and tutor support to fit around your schedule. You'll complete theory online and attend practical assessments to gain hands-on confidence.<br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_row_h7qVTJ": {
          "type": "accordion_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What is theaverage salary for a Personal Trainer in the UK in 2026?",
            "row_content": "<p>Earnings can vary depending on experience, location, employment type, and client base:</p><p><br/>•\tEntry-level (gym-employed): £20,000–£30,000 per year (often with commission on sessions).<br/>•\tAverage across the UK: £27,000–£35,000 (employed or early freelance).<br/>•\tExperienced/self-employed: £40,000–£60,000+ (with a solid client roster).<br/>•\tTop earners (specialised, London-based, or high-end freelance): £60,000–£80,000+ (charging £50–£100+ per session).</p><p><br/>Freelance PTs often earn more overall (keeping 100% of session fees after expenses) but face variable income initially. Factors like location (higher in London/South East), specialisations (e.g., nutrition, pre/post-natal), and online training boost potential. Many Study Active graduates report doubling their previous salary within 1–2 years.<br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_row_AXjDyG": {
          "type": "accordion_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can I study the Personal Trainer course fully online?",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes - Study Active offers flexible blended learning: comprehensive online theory modules (anatomy, programming, nutrition basics, business skills) plus optional in-person practical assessments for certification. This meets CIMSPA standards while allowing you to study around work or family.<br/><br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_row_DkqUqw": {
          "type": "accordion_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do I need insurance to work as a Personal Trainer?",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes - public liability insurance is essential (and often required by gyms or clients) to protect against claims of injury or negligence. Costs start around £50–£150/year depending on coverage.<br/>Most CIMSPA-endorsed qualifications make you eligible for affordable policies through specialist providers. Study Active guides graduates on insurance requirements during the course.<br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_row_CMxgmy": {
          "type": "accordion_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What if I want to specialise (e.g., in nutrition, sports performance, or older adults)?",
            "row_content": "<p>Start with your core Level 3 Personal Training qualification, then add Level 3 or 4 specialist diplomas (e.g., Sports Nutrition, Exercise for Long-term Conditions). These open higher-paying niches and allow premium pricing.</p><p><br/>Study Active offers pathways to these advanced qualifications, helping you stand out and increase earnings.<br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_row_Ra8WMq": {
          "type": "accordion_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can I become aPersonal Trainer if I'm changing careers later in life?",
            "row_content": "<p>Absolutely — many PTs start in their 30s, 40s, or beyond. No upper age limit exists, and life experience (communication, empathy) is a huge asset. Our courses are designed for career changers, with flexible pacing and supportive tutors.</p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_row_k8kfNx": {
          "type": "accordion_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How do I get clients when I first qualify?",
            "row_content": "<p>Build gradually:<br/><br/>•\tStart in a gym for built-in clients and mentorship.<br/>•\tUse social media, free trials, referrals, and local networking.<br/>•\tOffer packages, online sessions, or corporate wellness.<br/>•\tStudyActive provides business modules, marketing tips, and graduate support to help launch your career confidently.<br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_row_iFRxiJ": {
          "type": "accordion_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Is the Personal Trainer qualification recognised internationally?",
            "row_content": "<p>CIMSPA-endorsed and Ofqual-regulated qualifications (like Study Active's) are highly regarded in the UK and often accepted abroad (e.g., Europe, UAE via eREPs equivalents). For full international work, check local requirements, but our certification provides a strong global foundation.</p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_row_pExgKk": {
          "type": "accordion_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do I need to be a member of CIMSPA or REPs?",
            "row_content": "<p>CIMSPA membership isn't mandatory to work as a PT, but it's highly beneficial for CPD, professional standards, job listings, and credibility. REPs (legacy register) has largely transitioned to CIMSPA. Many gyms prefer or require CIMSPA affiliation.</p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_row_T9A4zX": {
          "type": "accordion_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What happens after I complete the course?",
            "row_content": "<p>You'll receive your certificate, be eligible for insurance/CIMSPA, and can start working immediately. StudyActive offers ongoing support: CPD resources, alumni network, job guidance, and access to further courses.</p><p><br/>Still have questions? Contact our team for personalised advice!<br/></p>"
          }
        }
      },
